BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm ($Bitmap tracks which volume clusters are allocated. The MFT's own allocation and growth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (are managed separately, with space reserved as an MFT zone to reduce fragmentation. Small) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (files can fit entirely in resident $DATA attributes, while larger files have nonresident) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (runs. Sparse and compressed attributes change logical-to-physical mapping and must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 608.0 Tm (interpreted using attribute flags and allocated sizes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (Directories use indexed attributes such as $INDEX_ROOT and $INDEX_ALLOCATION, permitting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (tree-based lookup and sorted enumeration. Hard links are represented through multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm ($FILE_NAME associations with file record identities. Security descriptors, object) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (identifiers and reparse points add metadata semantics not captured by a simple FAT-like) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 510.0 Tm (directory record.) Tj ET
