BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (for consistency recovery. The volume dirty bit, update-sequence fixups, metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (redundancy and transactional logging serve different purposes. NTFS does not guarantee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (that all ordinary file data is journalled, and MFT mirroring covers only selected critical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 608.0 Tm (records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (Recovery requires considering log state, record sequence numbers, reference validity, MFT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (allocation, attribute lists, runlists and directory indexes. Chkdsk-like structural repair) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (may be needed for damage beyond ordinary log replay. A cross-platform writer must not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (alter a hibernated or fast-startup Windows volume as though it were cleanly unmounted.) Tj ET
